      "title": "Two moves",
      "beats": [
        {
          "key": "b01",
          "kind": "overview",
          "intent": "Name the two moves before showing them, on the graph the course uses.",
          "narration": [
            "Dijkstra's algorithm finds the cheapest path when every edge has a weight.",
            "It repeats two moves: settle the closest vertex, then relax the edges that leave it."
          ],
          "on_screen": [
